Golden Signals (SRE Fundamentals)

🔹 What are Golden Signals? ⭐
 Golden Signals are 4 key metrics used to monitor the health of any production system.
 They help you quickly understand if your system is performing well or failing.

🔹 Why it matters in real-world? 🏗️
 Instead of tracking hundreds of metrics, engineers focus on these core signals to detect issues fast 🚨
 👉 These are widely used in SRE practices (popularized by Google)

🔹 The 4 Golden Signals: ⚡
✔ Latency ⏱️
Time taken to respond to a request
 👉 Example: API response time = 200ms
✔ Traffic 📈
Number of requests coming to the system
 👉 Example: 1000 requests per second
✔ Errors ❌
Number of failed requests
 👉 Example: HTTP 500 errors
✔ Saturation 🔥
Resource usage (CPU, memory, etc.)
 👉 Example: CPU usage = 90%

🔹 Real Production Importance: 💡
Imagine your application slows down 🐢
👉 Latency → High (slow response)
 👉 Traffic → Normal
 👉 Errors → Increasing
 👉 Saturation → CPU at 95% 🚨
✅ Root cause → System is overloaded
👉 These 4 signals quickly help you identify and diagnose issues

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ Latency = Speed ⏱️
 ✔ Traffic = Load 📈
 ✔ Errors = Failures ❌
 ✔ Saturation = Resource usage 🔥
 ✔ Together = System health snapshot
